# Stage-level fork filter (Migration 74). Bare predicate — compose it into a
# WHERE clause (or after AND) at any site that joins
# `journey_chain jc` -> `rev.dispatches d` -> `rev.dispatch_intent_bindings`.
# Aliases `jc` and `d` are required at the compose site.
#
# Semantics: when a chain edge carries a fork point (`jc.fork_cutoff_ord`
# NOT NULL on the predecessor's row), only admit that journey's bindings
# whose producing dispatch belongs to a stage strictly BEFORE the fork stage
# ("fork AT stage N" = redo N; inherit ord < N). A dispatch's producing stage
# ord is the MAX over its dispatch_stages (a dispatch batching several stages
# is attributed to its latest pane — conservative across a fork boundary).
# A dispatch with no dispatch_stages rows (shouldn't occur) is conservatively
# excluded across a forked edge via the sentinel COALESCE. Plain chain edges
# (fork_cutoff_ord NULL) admit everything — pre-fork behavior exactly.
(
    jc.fork_cutoff_ord IS NULL
    OR COALESCE((
        SELECT MAX(fps.ord)
        FROM rev.dispatch_stages fds
        JOIN rev.playbook_stages fps ON fps.id = fds.playbook_stage_id
        WHERE fds.dispatch_id = d.id
    ), 2147483647) < jc.fork_cutoff_ord
)
